<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <!-- meta tags -->
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <!-- My Style Sheets -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/BaseCaseStudy.css">
    <!-- Imported things -->
    <script src="https://kit.fontawesome.com/28bb5a582e.js" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>

    <title>Title</title>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <div class="opening">
            <!-- Make this h1 bigger -->
            <h1>Full Case Study Title</h1>
            <p>Designer: Grace Lewis</p> <!--If other's contributed, list them here-->
        </div>
        <div class="problemStatement">
            <h1>Problem Statement</h1>
            <p>What problem are we trying to solve?</p>
        </div>
    </header>
    <main>
        <div class="objectivesAndGoals">
            <h2>Objectives & Goals</h2>
            <div class="objectivesBox">
                <div class="whatObjectives">
                    <div class="myObjectives">
                        <h3>My Objectives</h3>
                        <p>What were/are MY objectives from a designer perspective? Keep it light here. Jist overviews</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="audienceObjectives">
                        <h3>Audience Objectives</h3>
                        <p>What will/does the AUDIENCE hope to get out of this? Keep it light here. Jist overviews</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="businessObjectives">
                        <h3>Business Objectives</h3>
                        <p>What does the BUSINESS want out of this? Keep it light here. Jist overviews</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="doClashObjectives">
                    <h3>Do these objectives clash?</h3>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Do these objectives clash? If so, how? What problems does this cause for each of the parties. Keep it light here. Jist overviews</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="theProcess">
            <div class="processHeader">
                <!-- The header and icons at that header -->
                <h1>Our Process</h1>
                <div class="processIcons">
                    <div class="processIcon">
                        <img src="../icons/compas_alt_light/Compass_alt_light.svg" alt="Compas" class="icon">
                        <p>Discover</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="processIcon">
                        <img src="../icons/sertificate_light/Sertificate_light.svg" alt="Person in front of a board" class="icon">
                        <p>Define</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="processIcon">
                        <img src="../icons/pen_light/Pen_light.svg" alt="A pen icon" class="icon">
                        <p>Ideate</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="processIcon">
                        <img src="../icons/widget_add/Widget_add_light.svg" alt="Widget with add icon" class="icon">
                        <p>Design</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="businessChallenges">
                <h2>Business Challenges</h2>
                <!-- go and get the bullet point you used in figma. I really like that -->
                <ul class="businessChallengesList">
                    <li>What exactly is the BUSINESS wanting out of this? What challenges can you see with implemting these things? What are their goals? What specifically did they ask you for? ECT</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="productUsersAndChanges">
                <h1>Product Users & Changes</h1>
                <div class="whoUsers">
                    <h2>Who is using this site?</h2>
                    <p>Who are our users? If you have specific Product users/ Product testers, this is where you talk about them.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="userNeeds">
                    <h2>User Needs</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Fuck the business, what do the user need? If it is a redesign what were their biggest problems with the original? If this is an orignial concept what ecatly are your user base looking to get out of this? What did they want? This will be more of an overview.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="userChallenges">
                    <h2>User Challenges</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>What exactly are the biggest challenges the user faces with the current design? What are the biggest problems the users saw at the begining of the project? Be specific</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="featuresAndFunctionalities">
                    <h2>Features & Functionalities</h2>
                    <p>What do you PLAN to do? What potental solutions do you see to the problem?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="competitorAnalysis">
                    <h2>Competitor Analysis</h2>
                    <p>What do the other guys do? Who are we comparing this to?</p>
                    <div class="thoughts">
                        <div class="thingsLiked">
                            <h3>Things that are liked</h3>
                            <ul>
                                <li>What do you and the users like about the competitors? What did they do well? The good stuff</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="thingsNotLiked">
                            <h3>Things that are disliked</h3>
                            <ul>
                                <li>What did you and the users DISLIKE about the competitors? What would you change? What was annoying? What could have been done better? Where were they lacking?</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="notableChanges">
                    <h2>Notable Changes</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>What things did you do that your competitors didn't? What are some of the ways you fixed problems?</li>
                        <li>If a redesign what notible changes did you make? Why?</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sketchesAndScreens">
                <h1>Sketches and Screens</h1>
                <div class="sketches">
                    <h2>Sketches</h2>
                    <div class="sketches">
                        <img src="" alt="">
                    </div>
                    <!-- Add the sketches. Probably clean them up a bit first -->
                    <!-- Also decide if you want to add any other process notes -->
                </div>
                <div class="screensBox">
                    <h2>Screens and Walkthrough</h2>
                    <a href="#" target="_blank">Link to the Figma walk through</a>
                    <!-- see if you can just put a video walkthrough or an inline walk through -->
                    <div class="screenCaps">
                        <img src="" alt="">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
    <footer>
        <!-- Do you need a footer? -->
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
